name o5-02-scramble-1
timeout 700
time 1999-03-24T21:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN O5, SORTIE 2 OF 10 - AIRFIELD DEFENCE: BATAJNICA, 24-26 MARCH 1999.
# THE ALERT PAIR INSTEAD OF THE PAIR ON STATION.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/o5-airfield-defence.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: o5-01-cap.fbm - identical but for the two `spawn` lines.
#
# THE ARENA, and every coordinate in it is [SET]. Batajnica lies at ~44.93 N 20.26 E [T4, approximate -
# doc/campaigns/o5-airfield-defence.md says so and this campaign does not improve on it]. FlightBox flies
# it under `--elev const` on a 0 m datum (the real field is ~80 m) and with NO TERRAIN MASKING (gap C4),
# so the Fruska Gora, the Danube valley and every mask a Serbian battery used do not exist here. The
# field's runway heading (110 deg) and length (3 000 m) are [SET]; nothing in this campaign lands.
#   the field       44.93000 20.26000, with the fuel farm, a hangar row, one hardened shelter and the
#                   runway aim point around it
#   the point defence  P-18 node at 20.24000 (on the field), S-125 at 20.16000 (7.9 km W), 2K12 at
#                   20.19000/44.95500 (5.7 km W, 2.8 km N), ZSU-23-4 at 20.25200 (0.7 km W)
#   the package     ingresses due east along 44.93 N from 19.60000 (52.0 km out) at 5 000 m and 450 kt
# Scale at this latitude: 1 deg of longitude = 78 800 m, 1 deg of latitude = 111 132 m [DERIVED].
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION, AND ITS DIRECTION. The package that attacked Batajnica was F-15C, F-117 and cruise
# missiles [T4]; FlightBox flies F-16s for all three, which is declared and not hidden. THE F-15C ROW
# EXISTS AND IS DELIBERATELY NOT USED, and the reason was MEASURED in this round rather than assumed:
# `modules/air/FBAirModule` composes NO FIRE CONTROL, so `FBState::FireControl` is never written and all
# three of FBPilot's weapon-employment gates stay shut. Measured: an `f15c` with four AIM-120 designates
# at t = 8.6 s at 18.64 nm, holds `eng_locked = 1` for 28 s from 18.6 down to 8.8 nm, and never posts a
# WeaponRelease. A catalogue row is ACCEPTED as a FLIGHT MODEL, not as a combatant.
# The defender is the MiG-29 the 127th "Knights" actually flew - so unlike O1 and O3 the substitution
# here is on the ATTACKER's side, and it makes the attacker WEAKER than history (no F-117, no cruise
# missile, no AIM-7/AMRAAM mix from a 160 km radar). A FlightBox Batajnica in which the field still
# loses says something WEAKER than 1999 did, not stronger.
#
# THE TWO LAYERS CANNOT BOTH BE LIVE, AND IT IS THIS CAMPAIGN'S STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURE - stated in every
# file because a reader who skips it will read every result backwards.
#   1. A FlightBox SAM site has NO IFF INTERROGATOR (`modules/ground/FBSiteModule`: "a battery has no
#      IFF interrogator in this tree") and an FBRadarContact carries no identity by construction, so a
#      battery engages the NEAREST FIRM TRACK in its envelope whoever it belongs to. An AIRFIELD is
#      exactly the geometry in which the friendly aircraft are the nearest track: O1 could lay its CAP
#      outside its own umbrella, O5 cannot, because the defenders live under it.
#   2. `missions/FBMissionRunner` ENDS THE WHOLE RUN at the first flight-monitor K.O. (`FirstFlightKo`),
#      and a mission-killed F-16 falls from 5 000 m in about 122 s. So an air engagement and a bomb run
#      in one file are not two measurements, they are one measurement and a truncation.
# The answer taken is the one a real airfield takes and the only one this format can express: the
# missiles are HELD while the fighters are up (`set emcon hold <offS> <onS>`, the briefed emission plan
# of round C26) and free when they are not. Sorties 01-05 therefore measure the FIGHTER layer with the
# belt briefed quiet; 06-07 measure the MISSILE layer with no fighter airborne; the chain 08-10 lets the
# campaign's own attrition decide which layer is left. THE CAMPAIGN NEVER MEASURES BOTH AT ONCE, and any
# claim that it did would be manufactured.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WHAT DOES THE SCRAMBLE COST? This is o5-01 with the pair's two `spawn` lines
# changed and nothing else.
#
# AND THE SCRAMBLE IS A DISPLACEMENT, NOT A DELAY, BECAUSE THE FORMAT CANNOT DECLARE A DELAY - measured
# in this round, not assumed. `set task intercept` sets the pilot's phase AT SPAWN (`FBF16Module` /
# `FBMig29Module` ApplySetup), and `FBPilot`'s phase machine has NO transition from Route into Intercept,
# so a `spawn ground` unit that is also given a combat task never runs Preflight/Takeoff/Climb at all.
# MEASURED on this arena: with a `runway` line the MiG steers off the strip and FAILs "touchdown off the
# assigned runway" at t = 11.1 s; without one it rolls, lifts and cartwheels - `monitor KO ...
# reason=ATTITUDE_CONTACT` at t = 35.4 s. THE ALERT SCRAMBLE, WHICH THE SPEC CALLS THIS CAMPAIGN'S MOST
# IMPORTANT SINGLE PARAMETER, IS NOT EXPRESSIBLE. It is reported in doc/campaigns/o5-airfield-defence.md
# and not built around.
#
# THE ARITHMETIC OF THE SUBSTITUTE, so the reader can check it. 60 s of the CAP's own ingress at
# 450 kt = 231.5 m/s is 13 890 m; at 78 800 m per degree of longitude that is 0.17640 deg, so the pair
# starts at 20.52640 instead of 20.35000. It is also LOW AND SLOW, because a jet 60 s off a runway is:
# 2 000 m instead of 9 000 and 350 kt instead of 450. THAT IS TWO CHANGES IN ONE LEVER and it is said out
# loud; the attribution run that separates them (position only, at 9 000 m and 450 kt) is not one of the
# ten and stands in the campaign's State section.
#
# MEASURED (fingerprint e3e4b10c79c7cf6f): THE SCRAMBLE COSTS THE ENTIRE ENGAGEMENT. ZERO radar contacts
# in 700 s over a 726 m closest approach; zero shots; BOTH strikers release and both aim points (`m2sa3`,
# `m2nod`) are destroyed. THE MECHANISM IS A THIRD DEFECT AND IT WAS PINNED RATHER THAN ASSUMED: the pair
# climbs at 25.0 m/s at +5.86...+6.13 deg of pitch, the raid sits at -3.1...-4.2 deg IN THE BODY FRAME at
# 57 -> 25 km (well inside the N019's +-6.0 deg RAD bar) - and `FBMig29Pilot` posts the GCI's WORLD-frame
# elevation (+2.83 deg) into a BODY-frame antenna command where the pilot's own search law would post
# -3.03 deg. The bar's lower edge lands at -3.17 deg and the raid stays 0.5-1.0 deg outside it.
# ATTRIBUTION, four runs that are NOT part of the ten (the displacement changes three things at once):
#   late only  (20.52640 / 9 000 m / 450 kt)   first contact t = 48.0   3 R-27R   1 Mk 84 on the field
#   low only   (20.35000 / 2 000 m / 450 kt)   first contact t = 24.0   4 R-27R   0 Mk 84
#   slow only  (20.35000 / 9 000 m / 350 kt)   first contact t = 21.0   4 R-27R   1 Mk 84
#   all three  (this file)                     NEVER                    0 R-27R   2 Mk 84
#   all three + GCI deleted                    NEVER                    0 R-27R   2 Mk 84
# NO SINGLE COMPONENT BLINDS THE PAIR, all three together delete the engagement, and deleting the
# controller does not restore it.
#
# RE-MEASURED 2026-07-29, AND THE THIRD DEFECT ABOVE IS FIXED. The GCI scan elevation is now converted
# against the pilot's own pitch attitude (doc/pilot.md 2.15, doc/modules/mig29/datalink-gci.md 2.2a):
# entered -2.754 / -3.027 / -3.661 deg instead of +2.891 / +2.832 / +2.331. THE SCRAMBLE NO LONGER COSTS
# THE ENGAGEMENT: first contact t = 48.0 s at 25.70 sm (was NEVER), both R-27R away by t = 106.3, and the
# exit code moves 3 -> 0 on an UNCHANGED mission file. The five attribution runs above are the pre-fix
# binary's and are kept as the measurement that pinned the defect; the "all three + GCI deleted" line is
# the one that still stands unchanged, because deleting a controller cannot be fixed by a frame.
#
# READING RULE (PRE-FIX): exit 3 expected, and the verdict is the DIFFERENCE from o5-01 in three numbers -
# `eng_detect_s` and `eng_shot_s` on the pair, the count of `sms RELEASE ... store=mk84`, and
# `mission OBJECTIVE ... deny release`. A pair that arrives late is not a pair that fights badly, and the
# file separates the two by changing nothing else. exit 2 would be a defect.

zone umbrella 44.93000 20.16000 35000 100 18000   # the S-125's published envelope, as geometry
zone field    44.93000 20.26000  6000   0  6000   # the terminal box: first entry is the time-on-target

net batajnica
  control m2nod
  link radio 60000 mast 8
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member m2nod
  member m2sa3 autonomy hold
  member m2sa6 autonomy hold
  member m2flk autonomy hold

unit m2kna
  team hostile
  flight kn1 1
  module mig29
  spawn 44.93000 20.52640 2000 270.0 350
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set brief_sort left
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 20 270 50 5
  set brief_gci 60 270 31 5
  set brief_gci 100 270 13 5
  wp 44.93000 19.40000 9000 450
  objective kill team friendly
  objective deny release team friendly
  objective survive

unit m2knb
  team hostile
  flight kn1 2
  module mig29
  spawn 44.94500 20.52640 2150 270.0 350
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set brief_sort left
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 20 270 50 5
  set brief_gci 60 270 31 5
  set brief_gci 100 270 13 5
  wp 44.93000 19.40000 9000 450
  objective kill team friendly
  objective deny release team friendly
  objective survive

unit m2stra
  team friendly
  flight st1 1
  module f16
  spawn 44.93000 19.60000 5000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 44.93000 20.16000 5000 450
  objective kill unit m2sa3
  objective avoid zone umbrella

unit m2strb
  team friendly
  flight st1 2
  module f16
  spawn 44.94500 19.60000 5150 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 44.94000 20.24000 5150 450
  objective kill unit m2nod
  objective avoid zone umbrella

unit m2nod
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 44.94000 20.24000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free

unit m2sa3
  module sa3
  team hostile
  spawn 44.93000 20.16000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon hold 1 3600
  set rounds 4

unit m2sa6
  module sa6
  team hostile
  spawn 44.95500 20.19000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon hold 1 3600
  set rounds 3

unit m2flk
  module zsu23
  team hostile
  spawn 44.93300 20.25200 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon hold 1 3600
  objective no_fire
  objective survive

unit m2ful
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 44.93800 20.25000 ground 0.0 0

unit m2hgr
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 44.93200 20.23500 ground 0.0 0

unit m2has
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 44.93500 20.27000 ground 0.0 0

unit m2rwy
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 44.92700 20.27500 ground 0.0 0
